---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="JCB Hydraulic Quick Couplers | Hydraulic Quick Couplings" description="Hydraulic quick couplers for JCB machines — ISO 7241 / ISO 16028 flat-face / ISO 5675 profiles, sizes, threads and selection notes for JCB fleets.">
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-night-green">Machine-Compatible Quick Couplings</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">JCB Hydraulic Quick Couplers</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">Source the right quick-disconnect couplings for JCB machines — attachment lines, implement outlets and service replacements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:text-navy-950 prose-h2:mt-10 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-a:text-brand-blue">
        <h2>JCB Machines and Their Hydraulic Quick Couplings</h2>
        <p>JCB builds backhoe loaders, telehandlers, excavators, skid steers and compact loaders. JCB machines use flat-face (ISO 16028 style) couplings on most modern auxiliary lines; older backhoes and certain attachments may carry ISO 7241 ball-lock couplings.</p>
        <h2>Coupling Profiles You Will Find on JCB Equipment</h2>
        <p>The table below summarises the quick-coupling profiles most commonly used across JCB machine families. It is a field guide, not a guarantee: verify the profile on your specific machine before ordering.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Machine family</th><th>Common profile</th><th>Typical sizes</th><th>Typical threads</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Telehandler auxiliaries</td><td>Flat-face (ISO 16028 style)</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>ORFS / NPT / BSPP</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Excavator auxiliary lines</td><td>Flat-face (ISO 16028 style)</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>ORFS / metric</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Older backhoe lines</td><td>Ball-lock ISO 7241 where fitted</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>NPT / BSPP</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h2>Selection Notes for JCB Fleets</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Modern JCB machines use flat-face couplings on auxiliary lines — the standard for attachment changeover with low spill.</li><li>JCB backhoes built before the flat-face era may carry ball-lock couplings; confirm the face type.</li><li>Thread ends vary by export market; specify the region when ordering.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Replacement and Service Guidance</h2>
        <p>JCB machines are highly configurable at the factory. Provide the machine model, build year and a photo of the coupling halves — JCB auxiliary kits vary by model and option.</p>
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>Do JCB telehandlers use flat-face?</h3><p>Most modern JCB telehandlers use flat-face (ISO 16028 style) couplings on auxiliary lines.</p><h3>Are old JCB backhoes flat-face?</h3><p>Older JCB backhoes often carry ball-lock ISO 7241 couplings; newer models use flat-face. Check the coupling face.</p><h3>Can I retrofit a JCB machine to flat-face?</h3><p>Yes — replace both halves on the hose and machine sides. It is a common upgrade that reduces spill and contamination.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-navy-950 p-8 text-center sm:p-10 lg:flex-row lg:text-left">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-white">Need Couplings for JCB Machines?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">Send the machine model, coupling profile or a photo — we confirm the match within 24 hours.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="rounded-lg bg-cta-orange px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-orange-600">Request a Quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
